meta {
  name: 25 read the stored history
  type: http
  seq: 25
}

get {
  url: {{host}}/.nlsearch-history/_doc/{{session}}
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

docs {
  Chat bots: sessions and history - read the stored history

  One document per session, holding the last 10 turns. Each turn is the prompt, the JSON the model answered with, and the outcome.

  The outcome line is what makes follow-ups work: after a search it carries the ids and names of the first hits, so a later "make it 22" knows which document is meant. After a failure it carries the error so the model can correct itself.

  The index is created on the first request that carries a session, so this returns 404 until then.
}
